+// Embedder-controlled, sticky suspension of compositor-thread
+// CoreAnimation commits, driven by scene lifecycle rather than resize.
+//
+// On iOS, every window on the phone display shares the process's CA
+// commit machinery with UIKit's own windows. A CATransaction commit
+// made on the compositor thread flushes ANY layer with pending layout
+// in that context - including UIKit's - and UIKit's Auto Layout engine
+// hard-asserts when touched off the main thread. Observed directly on
+// device: during a background-to-foreground transition, the
+// compositor's CommitToScreen picked up UITextEffectsWindow's (the
+// keyboard window's) pending layout and the app died with
+// NSInternalInconsistencyException in
+// _AssertAutoLayoutOnAllowedThreadsOnly.
+//
+// While latched, commits accumulate as mCommitPending inside the layer
+// root and are flushed through the ordinary main-thread path on
+// resume. Deliberately per-window: windows hosted on the CarPlay
+// display, or feeding Picture in Picture, must keep committing while
+// the phone scene is inactive - the embedder simply never latches
+// those.
